// Customer, Store, Distribution Centre, Promotion, Return Reason (Stage 2.3 T2/T3) —
// single-level conformed dimensions, no drill hierarchy. Each dimension's descriptive
// attributes bind through a table-backed `def map` (key -> attribute) + an `md2db_map`
// (model/binding/md2db.ttrm) — the same mechanism the Product hierarchy uses, since
// md2db has no `md2db_dimension` construct and the wide cubelet binds only grain KEYS.
//
// Customer.state is the customer's HOME state (c_current_addr_sk -> customer_address.ca_state),
// reached via a two-hop CustomerCode -> AddressCode -> State chain because an md2db_map
// targets a single table and those two columns live on customer / customer_address. This is
// distinct from query #11 (revenue_by_customer_state), which slices by the BILLING address
// at sale time (each fact's own addr_sk) — a fact-level view kept in raw SQL, not a Customer
// dimension attribute. Customer.birthYear binds c_birth_year directly; age is derived at
// query time (:year - birth_year, #12).

def dimension Customer {
    key: customerCode,
    attributes: [
        def attribute customerCode { domain: md.CustomerCode, isKey: true },
        def attribute state        { domain: md.State },
        def attribute birthYear    { domain: md.BirthYear }
    ]
}

// Customer descriptive/geographic attribute maps (table-backed, N:1; bound in md2db.ttrm).
